# Tests of vi.kkl, run in examples/ (see examples/README.md). Its output is
# not a terminal here: it draws nothing and prints its messages, and the
# keys come from a file (Esc is the byte 0x1b in it). :p and :%p print
# the text; no case writes a file.

# moves: counts, $, w and b over UTF-8 text, r, x, i, and p of a character
$ testdata/vi.txt < testdata/vi-move.keys
"testdata/vi.txt" 4L, 71B
naïve café au lai
naïXe café au lai
naïXe café au Zlai
aïXe café au Zlai
ukel's viK
ukel's viK
	tabs and words: here, there
aïXe café au Zlai
ast line

# insert mode: A I o O, Backspace (not past the start), Enter, Esc; u undoes the last insert
$ testdata/vi.txt < testdata/vi-insert.keys
"testdata/vi.txt" 4L, 71B
Kukel's vi!
A Kukel's vi!
A Kukel's vi!
above
new line
	tabs and words: here, there
naïve café au lait
last line
A Kukel's vi!
x
yabove 
new line
	tabs and words: here, there
naïve café au lait
last line
A Kukel's vi!
above 
new line
	tabs and words: here, there
naïve café au lait
last line

# lines: dd with a count, P, yy p, J, u twice (the second takes the undo back), G with a count, :N
$ testdata/vi.txt < testdata/vi-lines.keys
"testdata/vi.txt" 4L, 71B
naïve café au lait
last line
Kukel's vi
	tabs and words: here, there
naïve café au lait
last line
Kukel's vi
	tabs and words: here, there
naïve café au lait
last line
Kukel's vi
Kukel's vi tabs and words: here, there
Kukel's vi tabs and words: here, there
naïve café au lait
last line
Kukel's vi
last line
Kukel's vi tabs and words: here, there

# search: /, n, N, around the ends, not found; Ctrl-G; an unknown command; :q refused after a change
$ testdata/vi.txt < testdata/vi-search.keys
"testdata/vi.txt" 4L, 71B
	tabs and words: here, there
	tabs and words: here, there
	tabs and words: here, there
search hit BOTTOM, continuing at TOP
	tabs and words: here, there
search hit TOP, continuing at BOTTOM
last line
Pattern not found: zzz
"testdata/vi.txt" 4 lines
Not an editor command: frob
No write since last change (add ! to override)

# a file that is not there yet
$ testdata/no-such-file.txt < testdata/vi-quit.keys
"testdata/no-such-file.txt" [New File]

# no file name: :w and :x cannot write
$ < testdata/vi-noname.keys
No file name
No file name

# wrong use
$ a b
! usage: kukel run vi.kkl -- [file]
exit 2
